      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T15:58:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this not need to do anything? Does Dawn automatically clean everything up when the wgpu::Texture stored in `texture` is deleted?\n\nThe super `ResourceProvider` is invalidating `texture` right after calling this, and if that\u0027s all that\u0027s necessary for Dawn, can we add a comment to that effect here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 92,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "b89975eb19ed30ad7a0ca17057136508bbadbcfd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f304937_2f9b9c7b",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnResourceProvider.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T17:45:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`wgpu::Texture` and `wgpu::TextureView` are currently released inside `BackendTexture::~BackendTexture()`. It\u0027s a bit different from Metal in that Metal\u0027s texture handle is released inside `onDeleteBackendTexture`.\n\nIs there any reason why we need additional `onDeleteBackendTexture` method instead of doing the cleanup inside BackendTexture\u0027s dtor?",
      "parentUuid": "276c7fae_bb8907e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 92,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "b89975eb19ed30ad7a0ca17057136508bbadbcfd",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "72f4c130_558ba19b",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnResourceProvider.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-01T14:32:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I want to say that it\u0027s to allow for OpenGL where the resource provider is able to work with the GL context to call `glDeleteTexture`, but it is more abstraction than seems necessary for the other backend APIs.\n\nI don\u0027t see why MtlTexture couldn\u0027t do its `SkCFSafeRelease(handle)`, but I also don\u0027t know the decision making behind that. I think once all the higher priority work settles down, we could revisit it and see if `onDeleteBackendTexture` is actually necessary.\n\nFor now, I think it\u0027s fine to have Dawn not doing anything inside onDeleteBackendTexture(), but I think a comment would be helpful to remind future readers.",
      "parentUuid": "5f304937_2f9b9c7b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 92,
        "endChar": 49
      },
